                "ImageDescription": {
                  "value": "A few pieces of dark cooking chocolate, looming from their packaging. This type of product is a cheap, somewhat coarse chocolate intended for cooking and baking, sold on the German market as „Blockschokolade“. This particular specimen was made by Müller &amp; Müller GmbH, Münchweiler (a subsidiary of Wawi Group), and has a minimum cocoa content of 40 %. The reflective blue-white packaging with giant letters is typical for cooking chocolate in the German retail market and is used in different forms by several brands.",
                  "source": "commons-desc-page"
                },
